Image fit ORIGINAL 4:3: the PS1's picture, filling the height, bars at the sides only.

Requested: an image fit called Original 4:3 with no black bars at the top and
bottom. Patch 0057's ORIGINAL 4:3 (a GAMEPLAY ASPECT label) showed the whole
240-line frame, and Crash 2 draws only rows 12..227 of it: its own blank lines
made black bands at the top and bottom of the picture.

ORIGINAL 4:3 is now fit mode 4 (PSX_PAUSE_FIT_ORIGINAL), and it is main.cpp's,
not the renderer's. present_set_fit() drives the renderer as letterbox, with
the game's blank lines (PSX_ORIGINAL_TRIM, "top,bottom" of 240 - the launcher
passes 12,12) trimmed in place of the configured overscan crop. The kept band
is the 4:3 frame less those lines, 40:27, and overscan_aspect_mul sizes it
without stretching, so the picture fills the window's height and the bars are
at the sides only. The other fits get the configured crop back
(g_overscan_crop). No renderer, D3D12 or dispatch change.

main.cpp:
- PSX_SCALING_MODE=original selects it; zoom and stretch are cleared with it;
- the Home menu's IMAGE FIT cycles ORIGINAL 4:3, letterbox, fill, fit width,
  stretch (the launcher's order). Picking it stages the 4:3 aspect too; a
  wider GAMEPLAY ASPECT ends it (letterbox), as in the launcher;
- menu_prefs_write writes "original"; the overscan keys and
  MENU_PREF_OVERSCAN of 0057 go, since the menu no longer changes the crop.

psx_pause_menu.c/.h: FIT_LABEL/FIT_NOTE gain ORIGINAL 4:3 ("THE PS1'S OWN
PICTURE, FILLING THE HEIGHT, BARS AT THE SIDES. APPLIES WHEN YOU RESUME.");
PSX_PAUSE_FIT_COUNT 5; 0057's aspect-row label (psx_pause_menu_set_aspect_
original) is removed - the aspect row reads 4:3 again.

The software (SDL renderer) path letterboxes by logical size and has no crop,
so there the fit shows the whole frame, as before.

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake.

